---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ContactCta from "../components/ContactCta.astro";

const aboutJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "ProfilePage",
  "@id": "https://maurizioturatti.com/about/#profile",
  url: "https://maurizioturatti.com/about/",
  name: "About Maurizio Turatti",
  description:
    "Twenty-five years of making technical decisions and living with the results. Architecture advisory grounded in direct experience building and operating software.",
  mainEntity: {
    "@type": "Person",
    name: "Maurizio Turatti",
    url: "https://maurizioturatti.com/",
    jobTitle: "Architecture Advisor and Company Co-Founder",
    worksFor: {
      "@type": "Organization",
      name: "SoftInstigate",
      url: "https://restheart.org",
    },
    alumniOf: {
      "@type": "EducationalOrganization",
      name: "Università degli Studi di Milano",
    },
  },
};
---

<Base
  title="About - Maurizio Turatti"
  description="Twenty-five years of making technical decisions and living with the results. Architecture advisory grounded in direct experience building and operating software."
  ogImage="/images/og-image.png"
  jsonLd={aboutJsonLd}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="/Maurizio_Turatti_CV.md" title="Maurizio Turatti CV (Markdown)" />
    <meta name="keywords" content="Maurizio Turatti, architecture advisor, technical due diligence, CTO advisory, architectural decisions, software architecture" />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="hero hero--first">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="hero-headline">The decisions behind the systems.</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="page-content section-stack">
    <div class="section-block">
      <div class="section-body section-body--lead section-body--spacious">
        <p>
          I have spent twenty-five years making and living with technical decisions. As a company co-founder, architect, and advisor I understand the problem, evaluate the trade-offs, and make the call that reduces risk without adding unnecessary complexity.
        </p>
        <p>
          Co-founder of <a href="https://softinstigate.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >SoftInstigate</a
          > and creator of <a href="https://restheart.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RESTHeart</a>, an open-source platform that turns MongoDB into REST, GraphQL, and WebSocket APIs with built-in security and a native MCP server for AI agents. What I learn from building and operating real software shapes every decision I bring to an engagement.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:12px; margin-top:16px;">
          <a href="/Maurizio_Turatti_CV.md" download="Maurizio_Turatti_CV.md" class="cta-btn cta-btn--primary">Download CV (Markdown)</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Selected work</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <div class="card-grid">
          <div class="surface-card">
            <p class="card-label">Luxury e-commerce</p>
            <p class="card-text">
              Multi-region delivery across Berlin, Geneva, and Shanghai. The challenge was not the technology. It was aligning distributed teams around a single architectural direction for a global luxury brand's e-commerce platform in China.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="surface-card">
            <p class="card-label">Retail, backend modernization</p>
            <p class="card-text">
              A system serving 2,600+ stores and 9,500+ terminals (141M+ documents, 1TB+ data) that was still working but had outgrown its original design. Throughput target exceeded by 79%, query time reduced 216x.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="surface-card">
            <p class="card-label">Mobility &amp; public sector</p>
            <p class="card-text">
              Traffic data platform (GART) for ACI group. 6+ national sources integrated through 18 microservices on AWS. 10,000+ events/day, 99.9% uptime since 2017. Serving HERE, TomTom, Radio24.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="surface-card">
            <p class="card-label">Public sector</p>
            <p class="card-text">
              Architectural discovery for a compliance platform at 400K+ entities and 9M+ API calls/hour at peak. The task was to identify where the actual constraints were and build a roadmap that prioritized what would make a measurable difference.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="surface-card">
            <p class="card-label">Enterprise content</p>
            <p class="card-text">
              RESTHeart adopted as core persistence and API layer for Crownpeak
              Content-as-a-Service, deployed on Kubernetes to thousands of enterprise
              clients globally. Architecture designed for long-term maintainability across a global client base.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="surface-card">
            <p class="card-label">Open source platform</p>
            <p class="card-text">
              RESTHeart: 2M+ open-source downloads, 10+ years in production.
              Agent-ready platform exposing MongoDB via REST, GraphQL, and
              WebSocket APIs with built-in security and MCP server for AI agents.
              Adopted by Fortune 500 companies.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">AI and architecture</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          AI amplifies the value of good architectural decisions, and the cost of bad ones. Well-structured systems benefit immediately from AI tooling. Systems with accumulated technical debt feel the pressure faster.
        </p>
        <p>
          I approach AI the same way I approach any technology: as a decision about integration, context, and trade-offs. RESTHeart includes a built-in MCP server for AI agents, because the architecture needed to support that kind of integration from the ground up. The question is always where AI creates value in a specific system, and what the architecture needs to support it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Career</h2>
      <div class="section-body section-body--spacious">
        <p>
          <strong>SoftInstigate</strong>, Co-Founder &amp; Head of Delivery
          (2014 – present)<br />
          Co-founded the company in 2014. Owned both the technical direction and the commercial relationship: business development, client engagement, pre-sales, proposal writing, and delivery. Product development and architecture advisory across automotive, retail, mobility, and public sector. Every engagement started with understanding what decision needed to be made.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Co-created <a href="https://restheart.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RESTHeart</a>, growing it from concept to 2M+ downloads and Fortune 500 adoption over 10+ years</li>
          <li>Designed and delivered GART (ACI group): 6+ national sources, 18 microservices on AWS, 10,000+ events/day, in production since 2017 with 99.9% uptime</li>
          <li>Led backend modernization for a retail platform: throughput target exceeded by 79%, query time reduced 216x</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>AKQA</strong>, Technical Architect, Berlin (2013 – 2014)<br />
          Enterprise digital transformation at a global digital agency. Delivered a luxury brand's e-commerce platform in China, coordinating distributed engineering teams across Berlin, Geneva, and Shanghai. The real challenge was making architectural decisions that multiple teams across three continents could align around.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Sourcesense</strong>, Delivery Manager (2011 – 2013)<br />
          Led a consulting team delivering open-source enterprise solutions across
          finance, telecom, and public sector. Technical decisions made in the context of commercial realities: timelines, budgets, and client expectations.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Alfresco</strong>, Senior Solutions Engineer, Italy (2010 –
          2011)<br />
          Supported the launch of Alfresco's Italian market operations. Pre-sales
          consulting and technical engagements for enterprise content management.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Earlier career (1997 – 2010)</strong><br />
          Enterprise integration, distributed systems, and software research: SOA architect at Sun Microsystems for Italy and
          the EMEA region, SOA/EAI consulting at SeeBeyond, founding an independent consulting practice as official
          partner for Sun Microsystems, and research in computational geometry and machine
          learning at the Università degli Studi di Milano. These roles built the foundation for how I evaluate technical trade-offs today.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Open source</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/SoftInstigate/restheart"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"><strong>RESTHeart</strong></a
          >: Agent-ready backend for MongoDB, built over ten years of architectural decisions aimed at keeping things simple and understandable. 2M+ downloads, Fortune 500 adoption. (Java, GraalVM)<br />
          <a
            href="https://github.com/SoftInstigate/facet"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"><strong>Facet</strong></a
          >: Data-driven web framework: turn APIs into HTML, zero code<br />
          <a
            href="https://github.com/SoftInstigate/ermes-mail"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"><strong>Ermes Mail</strong></a
          >: Async e-mail library and CLI for Java<br />
          <a href="https://github.com/mkjsix" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >All projects on GitHub →</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Writing</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          <a href="/writing/the-system-is-working"
            ><strong>The system is working. That is the problem.</strong></a
          >
          (Jun 2026)<br />
          <a
            href="https://medium.com/softinstigate-team/facet-a-different-approach-to-web-development-af884abe0b69"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            ><strong>Facet: A Different Approach to Web Development</strong></a
          >
          (Jan 2026)<br />
          <a
            href="https://medium.com/softinstigate-team/mongodb-deprecates-data-api-and-https-endpoints-how-restheart-can-help-58ea0c44660d"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            ><strong>MongoDB Deprecates Data API: How RESTHeart Can Help</strong></a
          >
          (Feb 2025)
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ContactCta subtext="info@maurizioturatti.com" />
</Base>
